.TH TR2PDF 1
.SH NAME
tr2pdf \- troff's output as PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tr2pdf
[
.BI -p " size"
] [
.BI -t " title"
] [
.BI -w " lwid"
] [
.B -l
] [
.B -n
] [
.BI -F " dir"
] [
.BI -d " x=v"
] [
.B -W
] [
.B -c
] [
.I file
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tr2pdf
reads the pages
.IR troff (1)
described (its
.I file
or its standard input) and writes them as PDF.
It embeds the fonts, OpenType (Libertinus's CFF) and TrueType, subset
to the glyphs the document uses, compressed, each with a map from its
glyphs to the characters they are, so that a reader can search and copy
the text.
It is a translation of Ali Gholami Rudi's Neatpost; with
.B -c
it writes what Neatpost writes.
.PP
Besides the text and drawing, it reads troff's device controls
.RB ( \eX' ... ' ):
.TP
.BI "papersize " w x h
The page's size, in points.
.TP
.BI "pdf " "file height"
Include a page of a PDF.
.TP
.BI "link " "target width height"
A link, from here, to a URI or
.BI # name\fR.
.TP
.BI "dest " "name " \fR[ page \fR]
A destination here (at the page's top, with
.BR page ).
.TP
.BI "outline " "level title"
A bookmark here.
.TP
.BI "folio " f
The page's number as printed: its label.
.TP
.BI "info " "key value"
The PDF's information
.RB ( Title ,
.BR Author ).
.TP
.BI "name " "name page offset"
.TP
.BI "mark " "title page offset level"
Neatpost's: a destination and a bookmark at a page and place given.
.PP
The options:
.TP
.BI -p " size"
The paper
.RB ( letter ,
.BR a4 ,
or its width and height in tenths of a millimetre).
.TP
.BI -t " title"
The title.
.TP
.BI -w " lwid"
Lines' thickness, in thousandths of an em (40).
.TP
.B -l
Landscape.
.TP
.B -n
Draw glyphs by name.
.TP
.BI -F " dir"
The device directory.
.TP
.BI -d " x=v"
Set a device variable.
.TP
.B -W
Embed fonts whole, not subset.
.TP
.B -c
Write what Neatpost writes.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tr2pdf
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1),
.IR mkfn (1),
.IR page (1)
